<TR><TD CLASS=contentSelected ID=Content TITLE=0>
We The Clans of The UnHoly Alliance in order to preserve, protect, and advance the causes of Chaos, Hatred and unmitigated Ultra-Violence, Hereby establish the UnHoly Alliance to strike fear into the hearts and minds of the Fascist do-gooders.
</TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=contentUnSelected ID=Content TITLE=1>
The Head of the UnHoly Alliance shall be known as the Executor, and will be Supreme Commander of all UnHoly Alliance forces, Leader of the High Council, Chief Law Enforcer, and head of the prosecution.
<BR>Among the powers the Executor shall be enumerated with:<BR>
	The Executor may<BR><UL>
		<LI>Execute prisoners at will</LI>
		<LI>Execute traitors at will</LI>
		<LI>Execute spies at will</LI>
		<LI>Manage personnel to meet needs as they arise</LI>
		<LI>Arrest</LI>
		<LI>Torture</LI>
		<LI>Establish breeding camps, outposts, and other fortifications
		<LI>Order atrocities to be committed and other crimes prohibited by international treaties, and decency
		<LI>Pass Summary judgments on entire populations
		<LI>Appoint Administrators to help in the administration of the UA
		<LI>Authorize mass executions</LI>
		<LI>Any means to carry out the edicts of  the council</LI>
		<LI>Vote in the Council to break a tie</LI></UL>
Among the Responsibilities<BR> 
	The Executor must<BR><UL>
		<LI>Carry out the edicts of the council</LI>
		<LI>Accept a specified limit on any power, that is specific and limited in duration</LI>
		<LI>Protect the UA</LI></UL>
The Powers and responsibilities of the Administrators<BR>
	Shall Be<BR><UL>
		<LI>To carry out the orders of the Council and the Executor</LI>
		<LI>Any power needed to carry out those orders</LI>
		<LI>To Sit on the council, to be at the discretion of the Executor or council</LI></UL><BR> 
The Executor may not be impeached, and chooses the positions successor.<BR>
The Executor May establish a guard for Executor’s own security<p></TD></TR> 
<TR><TD CLASS=contentUnSelected ID=Content TITLE=2>
The High Council shall be composed of the appointees of the various clans, administrators, and the Executor.  The Council except when explicitly not prohibited form doing in this constitution may act in its own accord.  However the Council is mandated from to refrain from interfering in the internal affairs of member clans, or deciding on any issue that can be made inside a clan, except in the case of gross incompetence of the clan, or extreme urgency if an emergency should arise.
The decision of the council is final and may not be appealed. Failure to carry out such an order is punishable by how the council deems fit.  If the Council decides on an issue that is forbade from their authority, the decision is null and void, and may be ignored upon the Executors determination that it was illegal.<BR> 
All decisions of the council will be simple majority to become official except in the following cases:<BR><UL>
	<LI>Impeachment of a fellow councilor will require 3/5 of the Council</LI>
	<LI>To order executions of UA members will be 3/5 of the Council</LI>
	<LI>To amend the constitution will be ¾  of the Council.</LI></UL><BR>
The Councilor’s shall have the following powers<BR><UL>
	<LI>The Power to command members of any other clans in the case of an emergency</LI>
	<LI>To arrest non UA members</LI>
	<LI>Any power needed to fulfill an edict of the council</LI></UL><BR>
The Council’s responsibilities are:<BR><UL>
	<LI>To negotiate treaties, and approve treaties</LI>
	<LI>To establish a currency</LI>
	<LI>To declare War</LI>
	<LI>To declare Peace</LI>
	<LI>To ensure the prosperity of the UA</LI>
	<LI>To ensure the downfall of enemies of the UA</LI>
	<LI>To review appeals of Clan trials</LI>
	<LI>To overturn a conviction of a wrongly accused member of the UA</LI></UL>
The Council must have 50% + 1 of its members to establish quorum.  The Council must vote on appointments of Administrators to the Council.<BR>
Councilors may not disclose information deemed  by the Council to be secret to anyone outside of the Council.<p> </TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=contentUnSelected ID=Content TITLE=3>
A clan is established with a simple majority of the council, and is assigned a duty of its choice among duties available.<BR>
The powers of the clan  are to<BR><UL>
	<LI>To deal with its own internal affairs as it sees fit</LI>
	<LI>To establish its own rules regarding conduct of its members internally</LI>
	<LI>To establish its own form of government</LI>
	<LI>To try its own members</LI>
	<LI>To appoint and remove its Councilor at will, in accordance of its own rules</LI>
	<LI>To complete tasks assigned to by the Council as it sees fit</LI></UL><BR>
The responsibilities of the clan are to:<BR>
	<UL><LI>To complete the tasks of the Council assigned to it</LI></UL><P></TD></TR>
<TR><TD CLASS=contentUnSelected ID=Content TITLE=4>
All Members of the Alliance have the following rights:<BR><UL>
	<LI>The right to be heard.  Any Member of the Alliance has a right to speak before the council.</LI>
	<LI>The right of appeal.  Any Member of the Alliance has a right to have his punishment reviewed before the council.</LI>
	<LI>Except in times of emergency, no Member of the Alliance may be executed without a trial before the Council.</LI></UL><BR>
Responsibilities of Members of the Alliance are:<BR><UL>
	<LI>Complete loyalty to the alliance</LI>
	<LI>To obey the Council and the Executor and those they have delegated power to</LI>
	<LI>To Prosecute the enemies of the alliance to the ends of the world</LI></UL>
</TD></TR></TABLE></TD></TR></TABLE>
